    "sample": " every year, so in one year, we have 3 times the number of houses in the park.\nThe total number of houses in the park is x, so we can set up the equation:\n2x + 3x + 3x + x = 300\nSimplifying, we have:\n2x + 3x + x = 360\nTo solve for x, we subtract 3x from both sides of the equation:\n2x + 3x + x - 3x = 360 - 3x\n15x = 230\nTo isolate x, we subtract 15x from both sides of the equation:\n15x - 15x = 230 - 15x\n15x = 60\nTo solve for x, we divide both sides"
